  Quick and dirty:  


  Refresh all your expired spells but one useless one (restore
ability is favorite).  Note that spell of detect unseen or a wand
of secret door detection will show the portal if it's within 8 
squares of you.

  The spell of cone of cold at skilled+ level does [XP/2 +1] d6
worth of damage to each of the monsters in a 9x9 square, centered
on the target square.  The target square can be up to 10 squares
away, but must be visible.  

  NB.  1. No effect on cold resistant monsters.  
       2. Double damage on fire resistant monsters.

  The effect actually occurs from 2 to 9 times.

  So, [(27/2) +1] d6 = 14 d6 = 42 average damage points.


  Imagine that on the plane of fire:

   42 times 9 monsters times 2 = 3864.  

  That assumes: 1. No cold resistant monsters (no damage)
                2. No fire resistant monsters (dbl damage)
                3. Absolute *minimum* number of effects.

  The effects also tend to "waver" around the target square,
so you can affect more than nine monsters.

  I'd say a reasonable amount of damage to expect from one
cast on a crowd of monsters on the Plane of Fire would be 5000.

  Most of that may be "wasted" in overkill, of course. ;^D




